3 is equal to 1000 kg/m\u00b3. Let me check that conversion.\n\nYes, 1 g/cm\u00b3 = 1000 kg/m\u00b3. So, converting the given densities:\n\n\u03c1_A = 2700 kg/m\u00b3 = 2.7 g/cm\u00b3\n\n\u03c1_M = 8900 kg/m\u00b3 = 8.9 g/cm\u00b3\n\nThat might make the calculations simpler since the mass difference is in grams. Alternatively, I can work in kg and m\u00b3, but since the mass difference is in grams, maybe using grams and cm\u00b3 is better. Let's proceed with these converted units.\n\nSo, \u03c1_A = 2.7 g/cm\u00b3 and \u03c1_M = 8.9 g/cm\u00b3.\n\nGiven that, let's write the equations again.\n\nLet V be the volume in cm\u00b3.\n\nThen, m_A = 2.7 * V (in grams)\n\nm_M = 8.9 * V (in grams)\n\nThe difference m_M - m_A = 60 g\n\nSubstituting:\n\n8.9V - 2.7V = 60\n\n(8.9 - 2.7)V = 60\n\n6.2V = 60\n\nTherefore, V = 60 / 6.2 \u2248 9.6774 cm\u00b3\n\nThen, m_M = 8.9 * V \u2248 8.9 * 9.6774 \u2248 ?\n\nLet me compute that.\n\nFirst, 9.6774 * 8.9:\n\nLet me break it down:\n\n9.6774 * 8 = 77.4192\n\n9.6774 * 0.9 = 8.70966\n\nAdding them together: 77.4192 + 8.70966 = 86.12886 grams\n\nSo approximately 86.13 grams. Let me check the calculations again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, 8.9 - 2.7 is indeed 6.2. Then 60 divided by 6.2: 60 / 6.2. Let me compute that more precisely.\n\n60 \u00f7 6.2: 6.2*9 = 55.8, so 60 - 55.8 = 4.2. Then 4.2 / 6.2 = 0.6774 approximately. So 9.6774 cm\u00b3, that's correct.\n\nThen 8.9 * 9.6774: Let's verify with another method.\n\n9.6774 * 8.9:\n\nMultiply 9.6774 by 10: 96.774\n\nSubtract 9.6774: 96.774 - 9.6774 = 87.0966. Wait, that's different. Wait, no, 8.9 is 10 - 1.1, so 9.6774 * 8.9 = 9.6774*(10 - 1.1) = 96.774 - 10.64514 = 86.12886 grams. Hmm, so same result. So about 86.13 grams.\n\nBut let me check if I made a mistake here. Wait, if I compute 9.6774 * 8.9:\n\n9.6774\n* 8.9\n--------\nMultiply 9.6774 by 9: 87.0966\n\nMultiply 9.6774 by 0.9: 8.70966\n\nWait, no, actually, that's not the standard way. Wait, 8.9 is 8 + 0.9, so:\n\n9