ial Condition**: \\( |x_{1}| = 99 \\) implies \\( x_{1} \\) can be either 99 or -99. To minimize the sum, we choose \\( x_{1} = -99 \\).\n\n2. **Recursive Relationship**: For each \\( n \\geq 2 \\), \\( |x_{n}| = |x_{n-1} + 1| \\). To minimize the sum, we choose the negative value for each subsequent term:\n   - \\( x_{2} = -98 \\)\n   - \\( x_{3} = -97 \\)\n   - Continue this pattern until \\( x_{100} = 0 \\)\n\n3. **Sum from \\( x_{1} \\) to \\( x_{100} \\)**:\n   - This forms an arithmetic sequence from -99 to -1 (99 terms) and \\( x_{100} = 0 \\).\n   - Sum of the arithmetic sequence: \\( \\frac{99}{2} \\times (-99 + (-1)) = -4950 \\)\n   - Total sum from \\( x_{1} \\) to \\( x_{100} \\): \\( -4950 + 0 = -4950 \\)\n\n4. **Sum from \\( x_{101} \\) to \\( x_{2014} \\)**:\n   - From \\( x_{101} \\), the terms alternate between -1 and 0.\n   - Number of terms from \\( x_{101} \\) to \\( x_{2014} \\): \\( 2014 - 100 = 1914 \\)\n   - Each pair of terms (-1, 0) sums to -1, resulting in \\( 957 \\) pairs.\n   - Total sum from \\( x_{101} \\) to \\( x_{2014} \\): \\( 957 \\times (-1) = -957 \\)\n\n5. **Total Minimum Sum**:\n   - Sum from \\( x_{1} \\) to \\( x_{100} \\): \\( -4950 \\)\n   - Sum from \\( x_{101} \\) to \\( x_{2014} \\): \\( -957 \\)\n   - Total sum: \\( -4950 + (-957) = -5907 \\)\n\nThus, the minimum value of \\( x_{1} + x_{2} + \\cdots + x_{2014} \\) is \\(\\boxed{-5907}\\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. The given conditions state:\n   \\[\n   |x_1| = 99 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |x_n| = |x_{n-1} + 1| \\quad \\text{for} \\; n = 2, 3, \\ldots, 2014.\n   \\]\n   We need to find the minimum value of \\( x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_{2014} \\).\n\n2. Let us square both sides of the absolute value condition:\n   \\[\n   |x_n|^2 = |x_{n-1} + 1|^2.\n   \\]\n   Knowing \\( |a|^2 = a^2 \\), we can replace:\n   \\[\n   x_n^2 = (x_{n-1} + 1)^2,\n   \\]\n   which expands to:\n   \\[\n   x_n^2 = x_{n-1}^2 + 2x_{n-1} + 1.\n   \\]\n\n3. Summing this equation from \\( n =